---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Refund Policy"
  description="Draft refund policy for ServiceNow Learn Easy."
  updated="14 November 2026"
>
  <p>
    This is a draft. No refund window, fee, or eligibility rule is final. Do not purchase a course
    until the approved policy is published.
  </p>

  <h2>Current status</h2>
  <p>
    Payment is not active in this preview. The final refund period and conditions will be decided
    before production payments are enabled. The owner must approve the policy and a qualified
    reviewer must check it against applicable consumer law.
  </p>

  <h2>Planned request process</h2>
  <ol class="space-y-2">
    <li>1. Send a request through the support channel with the order ID and account email.</li>
    <li>2. The payment state and course activity will be checked.</li>
    <li>3. The decision and reason will be recorded.</li>
    <li>4. Approved refunds are returned through the original payment method.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What will be considered</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Whether the request is inside the approved refund period.</li>
    <li>The payment and enrollment state.</li>
    <li>Whether a technical fault prevented access.</li>
    <li>Whether the course was substantially used or shared.</li>
    <li>Applicable consumer protection requirements.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Chargebacks and disputes</h2>
  <p>
    A payment dispute may suspend access while it is reviewed. Access may be restored if the dispute
    is resolved in the student's favour. Fraudulent disputes may lead to account closure.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> for refund questions. Never send card details in a
    message.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
